  "query_preview": "..Today...Our upper-level low from the past couple of\ndays has moved eastward into New Mexico. Lingering moisture will \nresulting in a few scattered showers and possibly a thunderstorm \nthrough this afternoon, primarily across eastern Arizona. Otherwise,\ndrier conditions and cool temperatures will prevail across much \nof the area.\n\nRiver flooding remains a threat along the Little Colorado River,\nwith many gauges reaching or expected to reach minor flood stage \nfrom St. Johns to Winslow. Refer the Flood Warning bulletins for\nthe latest information.\n\nThursday through Sunday...In the wake of the low, heights begin to \nrise across Arizona as high pressure builds back into the region. \nWarmer, more seasonable temperatures ensue as a result. Dry \nconditions also look to prevail through at least the weekend.\n\nMonday onward...Uncertainly looks to remain in any potential \nmoisture increase early next week. There is a potential for \nHurricane Rachel to initiate a surge of sub-tropical moisture up the \nCalifornia Baja, however ensemble guidance does not seem too \noptimistic about this. While at the same time, a weak shortwave \nlooks to move into the Great Basin.",
